WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.916 --> 00:00:29.958


2
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.416
<b>Here, Lord Krishna says,</b>

3
00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:33.791
<b>"O Arjuna!</b>

4
00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:36.333
<b>This soul resides in every being</b>

5
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:38.250
<b>and it is indestructible</b>

6
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.750
<b>meaning it cannot be slain.</b>

7
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.833
<b>Therefore,</b>

8
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:47.375
<b>you should not grieve for any living being."</b>

9
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:52.250


10
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:58.250
<b>Lord Krishna is here summarizing the key points</b>
<b>He has presented in the previous verses.</b>

11
00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.291
<b>First:</b>

12
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.458
<b>The soul is indestructible.</b>

13
00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:02.416
<b>Second:</b>

14
00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:04.916
<b>It dwells within all living beings.</b>

15
00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:06.291
<b>And third:</b>

16
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:09.833
<b>Arjuna should not grieve over anyone's death.</b>

17
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:12.333
<b>This point has been emphasized repeatedly</b>

18
00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:13.208
<b>because</b>

19
00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:17.416
<b>death is what causes the deepest sorrow.</b>

20
00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:21.833
<b>After all, isn't this the very source of</b>
<b>Arjuna's despair?</b>

21
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.916


22
00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:31.250
<b>Grief and regret upon death.</b>

23
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:38.250
<b>Grief over why our loved one left us behind.</b>

24
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.750
<b>Regret</b>

25
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.083
<b>over countless moments from the past.</b>

26
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:46.083
<b>If only we had said this to them,</b>

27
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:48.708
<b>if only we hadn't said that,</b>

28
00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:53.500
<b>if only we had spent more time with them.</b>

29
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.583
<b>Such thoughts are only natural for humans</b>
<b>when faced with someone's death.</b>

30
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:00.500
<b>However,</b>

31
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.875
<b>it's essential</b>

32
00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:08.541
<b>that these clouds of grief and</b>
<b>regret linger only for a time.</b>

33
00:02:08.541 --> 00:02:18.041
<b>Let them not become so dense, so dark that they</b>
<b>devour the sun within us,</b>

34
00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:23.125
<b>pushing our life towards darkness.</b>

35
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.125
<b>Think about it</b>

36
00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:28.666
<b>would the loved one who has passed</b>

37
00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:35.208
<b>ever want to see you in such a state?</b>

38
00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:36.625
<b>In times like these,</b>

39
00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.541
<b>this knowledge of the soul,</b>

40
00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:43.250
<b>these teachings of the Gita,</b>
<b>will be your guide.</b>

41
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:48.250
<b>They will keep your inner sun so bright</b>

42
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:55.500
<b>that the clouds of grief and</b>
<b>regret cannot overshadow it.</b>

43
00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.583
<b>To completely abandon emotions</b>

44
00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:04.833
<b>is neither desirable nor possible for humans.</b>

45
00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:10.625
<b>After all, it's these very emotions that</b>
<b>inspire us to do good.</b>

46
00:03:10.625 --> 00:03:13.333
<b>They are necessary.</b>

47
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:19.250
<b>One should certainly experience their emotions,</b>

48
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.166
<b>but</b>

49
00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:26.833
<b>simultaneously remain capable of</b>
<b>maintaining control over them.</b>

50
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:32.166
<b>And it is in achieving this capability that</b>
<b>these teachings will support you.</b>

51
00:03:32.791 --> 00:03:36.916


52
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:40.750
<b>What do you think</b>

53
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:46.833
<b>Arjuna, in his current state of</b>
<b>distress and anguish</b>

54
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:55.500
<b>if someone were to simply tell him</b>
<b>without any knowledge</b>

55
00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:01.541
<b>or context to "abandon grief," could he do it?</b>

56
00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:08.833
<b>Would his mind understand why grief is futile?</b>

57
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:10.458
<b>In family situations,</b>

58
00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:16.375
<b>we often make the mistake of treating</b>
<b>mere instructions as wisdom.</b>

59
00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:18.416
<b>Especially when</b>

60
00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:22.416
<b>we're speaking to someone younger.</b>

61
00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:25.333
<b>"You shouldn't cry like this,"</b>

62
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:27.250
<b>"Don't do that," </b>

63
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.708
<b>"Stop going outside,"</b>

64
00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.333
<b>"That's not the right way."</b>

65
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:33.958
<b>These are all instructions,</b>

66
00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:36.125
<b>not wisdom.</b>

67
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:40.833
<b>If we truly want to help someone,</b>

68
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:46.583
<b>we must explain the reasoning</b>
<b>behind our instructions,</b>

69
00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:50.375
<b>provide them with proper guidance,</b>

70
00:04:50.375 --> 00:04:53.250
<b>share complete knowledge.</b>

71
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.083
<b>And when we do this,</b>

72
00:04:56.083 --> 00:05:03.416
<b>our words will no longer seem like hollow</b>
<b>commands but meaningful lessons.</b>

73
00:05:03.416 --> 00:05:04.916
<b>Through this process,</b>

74
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:12.458
<b>even the youngest among us will develop the</b>
<b>ability to find solutions to their own problems.</b>

75
00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:15.083
<b>Don't just give instructions</b>

76
00:05:15.083 --> 00:05:18.208
<b>explain the reasoning behind them.</b>

77
00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:21.208
<b>Don't just share words</b>

78
00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:25.125
<b>share the wisdom behind them.</b>

79
00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:29.875


80
00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:33.625
<b>Arjuna's despair is necessary,</b>

81
00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:37.791
<b>his doubts are necessary.</b>

82
00:05:37.791 --> 00:05:41.000
<b>My purpose now is</b>

83
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:48.875
<b>to resolve his despair and all his</b>
<b>doubts through proper knowledge.</b>

84
00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:56.708
<b>I do not wish to merely instruct him to fight.</b>

85
00:05:56.708 --> 00:05:58.250
<b>If I did so,</b>

86
00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:02.666
<b>this decision would be mine, not his.</b>

87
00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:06.750
<b>I want him to understand the right knowledge,</b>

88
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.833
<b>and reach this conclusion himself</b>

89
00:06:10.833 --> 00:06:13.125
<b>that he should not grieve,</b>

90
00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>that he must fulfill his duty in</b>
<b>this war with full valor.</b>

91
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:19.750
<b>A decision made by oneself</b>

92
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:25.708
<b>is far more powerful than following</b>
<b>someone else's instructions.</b>

93
00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:31.875
<b>This is a profound lesson for professional life.</b>

94
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:36.666
<b>When you only give instructions</b>
<b>to your colleagues,</b>

95
00:06:36.666 --> 00:06:39.750
<b>the work may get done,</b>

96
00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.291
<b>but</b>

97
00:06:41.291 --> 00:06:47.166
<b>gradually they become dependent</b>
<b>on your directives.</b>

98
00:06:47.166 --> 00:06:50.833
<b>They don't feel ownership of the work</b>

99
00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:56.666
<b>because they're merely following orders.</b>

100
00:06:56.666 --> 00:06:59.375
<b>Two things are essential.</b>

101
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:00.333
<b>First</b>

102
00:07:00.333 --> 00:07:05.333
<b>They should take responsibility themselves,</b>
<b>not remain dependent on you</b>

103
00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:06.875
<b>Second</b>

104
00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:12.541
<b>They should become capable of</b>
<b>solving their own problems.</b>

105
00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:14.166
<b>For this, it's necessary</b>

106
00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:19.958
<b>that you adopt the path of</b>
<b>guidance, not instruction.</b>

107
00:07:19.958 --> 00:07:22.583
<b>Give them the right knowledge,</b>

108
00:07:22.583 --> 00:07:28.916
<b>and let them reach their own conclusions,</b>
<b>make their own decisions.</b>

109
00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:30.250
<b>By doing this,</b>

110
00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:34.583
<b>gradually both their sense of responsibility</b>

111
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:39.291
<b>and their problem solving abilities will grow.</b>

